WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.740
There is a planet orbiting a G-type main sequence
star.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:12.480
It is in what scientists call the Goldilocks
zone - capable of sustaining life, unlike

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.570
the millions of barren rocks littering the
cosmos.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.860
And life does more than survive on this world
- it thrives there.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.600
The large world is home to a diverse mix of
animal and plant life, including a large,

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.460
technologically advanced civilization of humans.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:33.910
Aside from Earth, it is the most complex ecosystem
the SCP Foundation has ever discovered.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:44.260
And it may be the greatest threat to life
on Earth in 

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:45.559
the universe.

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:48.630
SCP-3003 - The End of History

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:49.630
Object Class - Keter

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:53.950
Research into this world, located roughly
208 light years from Earth, discovered many

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.129
similarities to our own world.

00:00:56.129 --> 00:01:00.930
It is only three percent heavier than Earth,
rotates in thirty hours, and orbits its sun

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.629
at a similar distance to our own world.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:08.110
The temperatures are similar, and temperate
enough so that the majority of the planet’s

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:11.529
land mass can support extensive life.

00:01:11.529 --> 00:01:18.709
While few species found on SCP-3003 are identical
to those on Earth, many are extremely similar.

00:01:18.709 --> 00:01:25.020
But three of these organisms combine to create
an existential threat.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:30.681
SCP-3003-1 is a small beetle-like creature
known as “Marce” by the planet’s human

00:01:30.681 --> 00:01:31.840
population.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.770
While they grow only to three centimeters
at most, they have a strong ability to defend

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:37.840
themselves.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.860
In addition to their hard carapace, they can
shoot a spider-silk-like substance from their

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:46.880
abdomen and coat themselves with an acidic
liquid to make them impossible for predators

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:47.880
to eat.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.399
They spend most of their time swarming and
feeding on plants, and can live fifteen years

00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:53.399
in the wild.

00:01:53.399 --> 00:01:56.270
They’re largely harmless to the planet’s
humans.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:00.579
That is, until an invisible enemy enters the
picture.

00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:06.399
SCP-3003-2 is a single-celled amoeba-like
creature that has evolved solely to parasitize

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:15.120
on other beings, and SCP-3003-1 is essential
to its life cycle.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.040
It makes contact with the Marce and infects
them - but it doesn’t stay there.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:26.780
Rather, it starts to transform the beetles
into vicious parasites that develop a long,

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.670
pointed stinger on the head.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:34.040
This stinger can paralyze its target, allowing
the Marce to inject it with the population

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.579
of SCP-3003-2 lurking inside it.

00:02:37.579 --> 00:02:42.739
And these transformed beetles only have one
target.

00:02:42.739 --> 00:02:46.120
SCP-3003-3 is humans.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.569
Thirty billion of them, in fact.

00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:53.680
The human civilization of SCP-3003 is far
larger than that of Earth, and studies have

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.379
indicated that they’re genetically identical
and could produce viable offspring with our

00:02:58.379 --> 00:02:59.379
own humans.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:05.680
And they are the primary target of the infection
of SCP-3003-1 and SCP-3003-2.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:11.561
When attacked by the infected Marce, the beetle
creates a hole and enters, sealing it with

00:03:11.561 --> 00:03:16.709
its silk material, and can live up to three
years inside the human.

00:03:16.709 --> 00:03:21.420
And in this time, the human is fundamentally
transformed.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:28.010
When infected, SCP-3003-3 becomes obsessed
with spreading the Marce, and develop a pleasure

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.870
response to being in its presence.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:35.510
They maintain their intelligence, but become
hyper-rational - able to evaluate information

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:39.349
quickly and effectively without any influence
of emotions.

00:03:39.349 --> 00:03:44.400
While the capacity for emotions remains, these
humans rarely express them and almost never

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.709
act on them.

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:50.510
They have one primary function - to spread
the infection further.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:53.150
It sounds like the beginning of an alien invasion.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:04:01.129
But the invasion already happened - and the
war is 

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:02.129
long over.

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:06.069
The infection is not growing - it is already
complete.

00:04:06.069 --> 00:04:12.390
SCP-3003 has a population of thirty billion
humans, and every single one is parasitized

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.870
by SCP-3003-1.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:19.880
This has happened centuries ago, and the entire
society has been reshaped to accommodate these

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:24.979
parasitic creatures and to make the human
population more hospitable to them.

00:04:24.979 --> 00:04:29.860
While these humans are identical to those
on Earth, they lack its genetic diversity.

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:36.040
The humans of SCP-3003 have been selectively
bred to made ideal hosts, complete with larger

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:41.949
bodies, more fat tissue, higher pain tolerance,
and less susceptibility to diseases.

00:04:41.949 --> 00:04:45.050
But the society has not degraded due to the
infection.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.280
Quite the opposite.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:54.199
SCP-3003-3 has become a hivemind of sorts,
working together for a single purpose.

00:04:54.199 --> 00:04:58.770
As such, these humans have evolved to be far
more united than humans on Earth.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:04.160
They all speak a single language similar to
Dutch, with no other languages active.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.780
All humans belong to the same culture, and
research has indicated this is about five

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:10.160
hundred years old.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:16.052
Before the infection, they were a humble society
that had over seven thousand cultures on it

00:05:16.052 --> 00:05:18.229
and mainly engaged in trading.

00:05:18.229 --> 00:05:19.730
None of them exist anymore.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:23.310
But they aren’t the only thing that’s
gone.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:27.629
SCP-3003 lacks Earth’s genetic diversity
in animal and plant life.

00:05:27.629 --> 00:05:34.000
That’s because in the early wave of SCP-3001-1
infections, the newly infected humans targeted

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.900
any species that preyed on the Marce.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:40.710
This led to mass extinctions that created
starvation and other ecological catastrophes

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:46.420
- and led to a massive change in the way the
humans of SCP-3003 life.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:51.610
The vast majority live in carefully planned
cities, built in the safe and temperate regions

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:52.610
of the planet.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:58.600
The cities are mostly enclosed and are used
for industry and food growth, and are tightly

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:02.560
built - so much so that SCP personnel reported
feeling claustrophobic.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:03.900
But one element of these cities was even stranger.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:07.909
Many surfaces of the cities are coated with
a material that closely resembles the feel

00:06:07.909 --> 00:06:11.930
of SCP-3003-1 - the Marce beetle.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:16.509
The infected are so fixated on the pleasure
that being around these beetles gives them

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:19.330
that they use this as a form of entertainment.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:24.691
The remaining members of this society live
in rural areas, in carefully planned small

00:06:24.691 --> 00:06:28.860
communities dedicated to farming, mining,
or manufacturing.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.449
These small pods are even more structured
than the cities.

00:06:31.449 --> 00:06:32.599
And every area of life on SCP-3003 is carefully
planned.

00:06:32.599 --> 00:06:36.530
Children in this world are raised communally
by large groups of workers specializing in

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:37.660
health and education.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:43.419
They are infected quickly - at only a little
over a year old, as soon as their supervisors

00:06:43.419 --> 00:06:45.889
are convinced they’re physically capable.

00:06:45.889 --> 00:06:50.460
Once they are infected and their mindsets
converted to the interests of the Marce, the

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:55.660
children are quickly tested to determine their
ideal occupation, and steered into what they

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.710
will do for the rest of their life.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:03.879
And like everything else on SCP-3003, day-to-day
life is highly structured.

00:07:03.879 --> 00:07:08.130
Adults typically spend ten hours a day at
work, with the rest being spent engaging in

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:13.419
basic activities like eating and sleeping,
attending educational classes, and engaging

00:07:13.419 --> 00:07:14.919
in entertainment.

00:07:14.919 --> 00:07:21.040
But the entertainment all revolves around
the society’s obsession with SCP-3003-1.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:24.970
They listen to recordings of the beetle swarms,
visit the enclosures where the beetles are

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:31.110
bred, or obsessively touch the distinctive
lumps that the parasites cause on their hosts.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:34.020
Everyone fits in on SCP-3003.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.039
There is no other option.

00:07:36.039 --> 00:07:40.810
Any sign of divergence from one’s job function
is cause for the authorities to step in.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:45.259
The first step is medical exams, to make sure
that the parasitic infestation isn’t becoming

00:07:45.259 --> 00:07:46.580
too harmful.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:50.610
Anyone who doesn’t conform to the social
standards is restrained by local members of

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.710
the hivemind and brought in for observation.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:58.730
When someone becomes too old or sick to work
for society and be a host for the Marce, their

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:04.330
usefulness is at an end - and they are used
for organ harvesting and experimentation.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:12.300
In the society of SCP-3003, one life has no
meaning - only its purpose to the hive mind.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:18.610
But one area of SCP-3003’s development is
of even greater worry to the Foundation - their

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:20.169
technology.

00:08:20.169 --> 00:08:26.070
SCP-3003-3 works as one, and that has allowed
it to develop technology far beyond that of

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:28.000
Earth.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:33.480
Their planet is run almost entirely on wind,
solar, and tidal power with an assist from

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:35.460
geothermal and nuclear power.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:39.550
Their computers have enough power to produce
data that makes foolproof recommendations

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:44.770
for public policy, and their artificial intelligence
systems are far beyond anything the Foundation

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:45.850
has developed.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:50.890
Their crops have been genetically modified
to have ideal hardiness and nutritional value,

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:55.930
and they routinely experiment on their own
DNA for selective breeding purposes.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:09:00.120
The planet has launched satellites into space
and visited the other planets in their solar

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.120
system.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:07.350
But it’s one invention that brought this
strange planet to the Foundation’s attention.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:14.160
SCP-3003-4 is a massive facility on SCP-3003
with one purpose - to open wormholes that

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:18.390
can transport members of the planet to any
other point in space.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:23.810
Each use of this device uses up more energy
than Earth uses in a full year, and the device

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:29.700
seems to have one main purpose - to transport
representatives to other planets that they

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:32.690
would like to expand their civilization to.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:36.910
The desire to spread the infection of the
Marce is a single-minded obsession for the

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:40.070
citizens of SCP-3003.

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:43.100
And they now have their sights set on Earth.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:48.610
Unlike most dangerous specimens, SCP-3003
and its native species were not discovered

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:49.610
in the wild.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:54.190
Rather, it made contact directly with the
earth through its wormhole generator, sending

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:59.150
ambassadors with one purpose - to spread the
gospel of their better, unified way of life

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:01.740
and to prepare us for joining their growing
empire.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:06.350
They could have passed for missionaries - but
what they were preaching was infection with

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:08.550
a parasitic mutated beetle.

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:13.520
The SCP Foundation was not prepared for this
first contact, and collected all the evidence

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:16.310
they could on this strange new society.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:19.120
They quickly came up with one conclusion.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:26.210
SCP-3003 was larger, more powerful, and more
advanced than anything on Earth - even the

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.190
SCP foundation.

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:32.280
With no other option for containing the threat
immediately, the Foundation took the only

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:36.770
approach they could - making peaceful contact
with the ambassadors and making them think

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:39.340
Earth was interested in what they were bringing.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:45.270
As long as the representatives of SCP-3003
think they are involved in a peaceful negotiation

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:51.170
for how to introduce the Marce to Earth, they
are ready to cooperate and agree to the Foundation’s

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.170
terms.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:59.770
This has given the Foundation the opportunity
to study some of this society’s weak points.

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:04.710
One weak point, in particular, may give humans
a chance for survival.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:10.540
The representatives of SCP-3003-3 do not know
how to lie.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:14.980
Once they’re converted to host the Marce,
everything they do serves a common purpose

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.700
and is shared with every other member of their
hive-like society.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:23.830
There is no need to lie and no purpose to
it in their society - and as such, they can

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:27.260
be deceived far more easily than humans.

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:31.720
That gives the SCP Foundation the chance to
stall them and fool them into thinking Earth

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:34.610
is planning for integration at its own pace.

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:39.360
But the patience of this strange civilization
may have its limits.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:44.020
The representatives seemed cooperative at
first, agreeing to many concessions the Foundation

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:49.230
requested - including carefully regulating
where they entered Earth and making the Foundation

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:53.530
their first point of contact for their Earth
Contact and Research Committee.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:59.350
This allows the Foundation to ensure no invasive
species make their entry onto Earth unknown.

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:03.470
Because the civilization is unable to lie,
the Foundation has convinced them that Earth

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:09.680
is contaminated and unable to host the Marce,
with the species becoming sterile when introduced.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:13.570
The representatives seem to believe this,
and believe they are working on a solution

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:14.710
with Earth.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:20.090
But some members of SCP-3003-3 may be becoming
more aggressive.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:26.500
It was after a meeting with a representative
of SCP-3003, and Dr. Shah entered an elevator

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:27.540
with the alien.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:31.600
Suddenly, the Marce host became aggressive,
tearing the control panel out of the wall

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.140
and stopping the elevator.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:39.120
Dr. Shah was terrified, but the representative
simply said it wanted some alone time.

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:44.800
The SCP-3003-3 representative started speaking,
but it didn’t seem to speak like the other

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:45.800
members.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.230
It was intense and intimidating.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:53.400
And most worrying, it referred to taking over
a two-legged species over five hundred years

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:54.400
ago.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:56.580
It wasn’t the human speaking.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:04.100
It was the single-cell organism that puppeted
both them and the Marce.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:09.310
Unlike the humans of SCP-3003, it wasn’t
fooled by the Foundation’s subterfuge.

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:14.140
It knew they were resisting, and it didn’t
believe the story about the planet being inhospitable

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:15.420
to the Marce.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:19.800
It wanted the Earth to surrender and join
the hivemind, and it argued Earth would be

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.230
better for it.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.430
No more war.

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:23.770
No more conflict.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:24.870
No more hate.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:25.930
No more poverty.

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:31.060
And all it would take was the complete surrender
of Earth’s free will.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:36.580
And it made clear that it would win.It would
be the last thing, the only thing left in

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:41.610
the universe - and everyone would join it
one way or another.

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:46.290
It was clear that the threat of SCP-3003 was
more pressing than thought.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:50.220
Which posed a question - How do you contain
a planet?

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:54.500
The decision to classify SCP-3003 as Keter
wasn’t hard.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:58.890
But none of the Foundation’s other tactics
would apply here.

00:13:58.890 --> 00:14:02.870
Investigation into the capacities of the planet
made clear that if a war was to break out

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:07.620
between the two planets, it would end swiftly
and decisively in favor of SCP-3003.

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:14.500
If the SCP-3003-2 living inside the bloodstream
of the planet’s humans were aware of the

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:19.130
Foundation’s deceptions, they did not seem
to be letting the humans of their planet in

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:22.620
on this - so the deception would hold for
now.

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:28.840
But SCP-3003 was moving fast as well - and
soon it might be too late to contain it.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:31.870
Two projects in particular concern the Foundation.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:38.200
One is a genetic tampering experiment to make
SCP-3003-3 more hospitable to their purpose.

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:44.900
It would add artificial genes to these humans,
making them consume less resources, be immune

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:51.500
to common pathogens, and make them able to
host ten times as many Marce.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.790
These genes would turn these humans into their
own species.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:59.460
At the same time, they are working on traveling
to and terraforming planets in other star

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:06.840
systems - which would make them capable of
spreading anywhere, and impossible to contain.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:10.960
But the Foundation has some last-ditch plans
to stop this.

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:15.220
In addition to continuing their disinformation
campaign, and researching the species involved

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:20.280
through samples of the Marce and the single-cell
being that mutates them, the Foundation is

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:23.440
preparing for the worst-case scenario.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:28.190
They are spreading disinformation among scientists
to ensure no additional contact is made with

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:33.390
elements outside the SCP Foundation, and the
O5 council has authorized studies into how

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:35.950
to eliminate this threat permanently.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:41.040
But the Foundation will only have one chance
to do so - and any attempt will need to involve

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:45.220
the elimination of their wormhole device to
keep them from escaping.

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:51.760
Because even one specimen escaping could mean
infestation of another world - and the threat

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.830
would begin anew.

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:59.550
But for now, the Foundation has not deemed
any plans for an attack to neutralize SCP-3003

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:02.070
practical or likely to succeed.

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:08.370
Which means the Foundation’s focus is on
maintaining stable relations with SCP-3003-3,

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:16.150
convincing them that we are moving towards
peaceful integration, and continuing to learn

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:23.330
all they can about this strange world - as
the SCP Foundation seeks to stall the end

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:24.630
of history.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:33.730
For more on terrifying insects, check out
“SCP-3004 - Insect God”, or watch this

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:37.190
video instead.

